# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke and prefix job of this pack (the prefix gate serves the selection in its containers too and fails an arm whose log lacks the checkpoint lines), so each pair
# differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# T1B (TIMED, the CANDIDATE of the pair): the ship-5 candidate c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5, a TRAFFIC profile whose owner waiver is PENDING
# (a profile whose decision does not start with APPROVED boots in a gate or a smoke and logs the word), the same tests as T1A, on Swift. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC
# runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. READ: c2_smoke_check clean AND python3 scripts/ci/octo_judge.py
# --container-log <container log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5 clean (the solo rule beside the octo rules); LEVER READS (the
# candidate's additions, on top of the ship-4 reads): NP1: octo_judge.py --container-log <container log> --profile
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5 clean (the solo rule: at least one "packed padded round live=1" line, no "packed padded skipped live=1
# eligible=1" line, beside the octo rules) and the NP1 lines in the container log: "[NP1] kv scratch: Qwen36ForCausalLM.allocate_kv_cache allocates 1 block(s) beyond the
# pool vLLM sized (pool 16500 blocks, scratch ids 16500..16500)" once, "[SOLO-PACKED] admitted min_users=1 scratch_pages=16500 (owner traffic waiver <id>)" once and, for
# each of the two M3 blocks, "packed padded block admitted min_users=1 users=4 max_idle=4 ... scratch_pages=16500"; the octo block's own admitted line is unchanged
# (min_users=6, max_idle=2, no scratch pages); EXACT RESUME: "[PINDIAG] prefix: window carry engaged undrop=1 carry=1" once (the scheduler graft's install line; a smoke
# without a salt never reaches it: agent_turns does, and window 2's prefix arm A2 holds the carried hits against cold twins); SLICED RESTORE: "host tier restore slice on
# blocks=512 ms=200" once; GRID13: the "tp4 grid13 engaged" line names all three sub-switches; TIER: the "host tier on" line says the 48 GiB budget and the 16 GiB
# checkpoint store; and the complete-spill mode's install line with its default knobs. PF2-H (the device-side hand-off of the final prefill step): "[PINDIAG] prefill
# handoff engaged" once, "[PF2] handoff mode=device ms=.. read_ms=.. write_ms=.." on every final step (the host path it replaces costs about 163 ms a final step in the
# ship-4 device profile: 48.6 ms of reads, 115.2 ms of writes), no "fell back" line, and on the audited twin "prefill handoff audit n=.. exact=True" for every audited step
# and no "audit mismatch": IT SHIPS ONLY IF THE AUDITED RUN PASSES. SCHED-1 (the lean admission, the complete spills, the trim): python3 scripts/ci/sched_report.py
# <container log> (and --second <T1B container> after <T1A container> for the pair): the rebind p50 and p90 of a returning turn (production: 541 and 721 ms; the lean split
# predicts about 240 ms), the lean split and phases, the read-backs skipped, the backstop reuses, the spill fit and counters; every figure prints - where no line is behind
# it.. Then: python3 scripts/ci/np1_report.py --control-a <T1A smoke> --arm-a <T1B smoke> --control-b <T1A smoke> --arm-b <T1B smoke> --arm-container <T1B container>
# --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5: np1_report is an ABAB reader and this pair has ONE boot a side, so each smoke is passed twice and
# the boot-to-boot floors read exactly 1 (no noise allowance): the ratios per test (the aggregate of the all-live window of the candidate over the control's) are the read,
# a GAIN at np1_live1 is the claim, and a LOSS the reader prints at a parity row for a difference of 2% to 5% is boot noise until a second pair (T1A T1B again, the owner's
# call) says otherwise. The texts must be EQUAL, user by user: python3 scripts/ci/octo_compare.py --control <T1A smoke> --octo <T1B smoke> --octo-container <T1B container>
# --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5: the same checkpoint, greedy, so a difference is a token the candidate changed and is NO-GO. AGENT
# TURNS: python3 scripts/ci/agent_turns.py report --smoke-log <T1B smoke> --container-log <T1B container> beside the same for T1A (agent_turns is judged by c2_smoke_check
# on each leg): the rates, the TTFT by context bucket, the tokens re-prefilled (the candidate's exact resume should re-prefill up to 2,048 fewer on a returning turn), and
# the per-turn answer hashes equal. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it.
# CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models
# answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through
# the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the
# lever. Duration (estimate): 45 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,np1_live1,np1_live2,np1_live4,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=95
